---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = "Trademark Registration Guide for Indian Businesses | BRNDNUR";
const description = "A founder-friendly guide to trademark registration in India: what can be registered, prerequisites, class selection, examination, and post-filing maintenance.";
const canonical = "https://brndnur.com/resources/trademark-registration-guide/";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  currentPath="/resources/trademark-registration-guide/"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <!-- Breadcrumb & Hero -->
    <section class="page-hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="bn-breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <a href="/resources/">Resources</a>
          <span class="sep">/</span>
          <span class="current">Trademark Registration Guide</span>
        </nav>
        <p class="eyebrow">Founders' Guide</p>
        <h1>Trademark Registration in India: The Complete Founders' Guide.</h1>
        <p class="lead">Everything you need to know about protecting your brand name, logo, and distinctive identity under the Trade Marks Act, 1999.</p>
        
        <div class="hero-badges">
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/></svg>
            <span>Trade Marks Act, 1999</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>
            <span>10-Year Renewable Protection</span>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-badge-item">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg>
            <span>PAN-India Statutory Exclusive Rights</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="actions" style="margin-top: 28px;">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/trademark-registration/">Apply for Registration &rarr;</a>
          <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/resources/">Back to Resources</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Guide Content -->
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container">
        <article class="legal-prose" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
          <div class="advisory-notice" style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 32px;">
            <div class="advisory-notice-icon">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"/><line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"/></svg>
            </div>
            <div class="advisory-notice-content">
              <h4>Quick Summary for Founders</h4>
              <p>A registered trademark confers exclusive statutory rights to use a brand identifier in connection with specified goods or services in India. Registration is valid for 10 years from the application filing date and is renewable indefinitely every 10 years.</p>
            </div>
          </div>

          <h2>1. What Is a Trademark?</h2>
          <p>Under Section 2(1)(zb) of the Trade Marks Act, 1999, a trademark is defined as a mark capable of being represented graphically and capable of distinguishing the goods or services of one person from those of others. It may include a device, brand, heading, label, ticket, name, signature, word, letter, numeral, shape of goods, packaging or combination of colours.</p>

          <h2>2. What Can and Cannot Be Registered?</h2>
          <p>To qualify for registration, a mark must possess distinctive character:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Strong Candidates:</strong> Coined or invented words (e.g., brand names with no dictionary meaning), arbitrary words (common words used in an unrelated context), or suggestive terms requiring imagination.</li>
            <li><strong>Challenging or Prohibited:</strong> Purely descriptive words describing the nature, quality, or geographical origin of the goods/services (e.g., "Fast Delivery" for a courier service), generic product terms, deceptive marks, or marks identical to prior registered marks.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>3. Prerequisites and Information to Prepare</h2>
          <p>Before filing Form TM-A with the Trade Marks Registry, ensure you have gathered:</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Applicant Details:</strong> Full legal name, nationality, and trading address. For firms/LLPs/companies, the registration certificate and Udyam MSME certificate (if eligible for 50% government fee concession).</li>
            <li><strong>Representation of the Mark:</strong> Clear word spelling or high-resolution logo artwork (PNG/JPEG format).</li>
            <li><strong>Date of First Use:</strong> Whether the mark is proposed to be used, or has been used since a specific date (supported by a user affidavit and commercial invoices).</li>
            <li><strong>List of Goods or Services:</strong> Accurate specification aligned with the appropriate Nice Class.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>4. The Statutory Application Lifecycle</h2>
          <p>The journey from filing to registration involves distinct statutory stages governed by the CGPDTM:</p>

          <div class="bn-table-wrap">
            <table class="bn-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th>Stage</th>
                  <th>Key Milestone</th>
                  <th>Legal Status</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <td>1. E-Filing</td>
                  <td>Form TM-A submitted & official receipt generated</td>
                  <td>Entitled to use &trade; symbol</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>2. Formalities Check</td>
                  <td>Registry verifies applicant details & Vienna code</td>
                  <td>Formalities Chk Pass</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>3. Examination</td>
                  <td>Section 9 & 11 review; Examination Report issued</td>
                  <td>Marked for Exam / Objection</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>4. Journal Publication</td>
                  <td>Advertised in Trade Marks Journal for 4 months</td>
                  <td>Public Opposition Window</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <td>5. Registration</td>
                  <td>Certificate of Registration issued by Registrar</td>
                  <td>Lawful right to use &reg; symbol</td>
                </tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2>5. Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
          <ul>
            <li>Skipping preliminary clearance searches before launching brand packaging.</li>
            <li>Selecting the wrong trademark class, leaving primary revenue streams unprotected.</li>
            <li>Filing as an ordinary corporate entity when valid MSME/Startup status could reduce official government fees by 50%.</li>
            <li>Missing statutory deadlines for responding to Examination Reports or opposition notices.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2>6. Statutory Official Sources</h2>
          <p>For official rules, fee schedules, and public search portals, refer directly to the Controller General of Patents, Designs and Trade Marks (CGPDTM) at <a href="https://ipindia.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">ipindia.gov.in</a>.</p>
        </article>

        <div class="cta-panel" style="margin-top: 48px;">
          <p class="eyebrow">Ready to Protect Your Brand?</p>
          <h2>Start with a Professional Clearance Review.</h2>
          <p>Our advisory team conducts thorough similarity searches and helps you navigate class selection and documentation.</p>
          <div class="cta-actions">
            <a class="btn btn-gold" href="https://wa.me/919048188899?text=Hello%20BRNDNUR%2C%20I%20want%20to%20register%20a%20trademark." target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inquire on WhatsApp &rarr;</a>
            <a class="btn btn-outline" href="/trademark-registration/">View Registration Services</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
